# Unit Tests (Ch.9)

Source: Robert C. Martin, _Clean Code_. Inventory: `docs/clean-code-inventory.md`. ESLint: `@vitest/eslint-plugin` recommended + `consistent-test-it` (`it`) + `max-expects` (4) on `*.{spec,harness}.ts`; Ch.3 size/`complexity` offs (dual standard). Ch.17: `jscpd` gates clones across `src` (including specs/harnesses) — prefer shared fixtures/helpers over copy-paste.

## Three Laws of TDD

Prefer a failing test before production behavior. Keep the suite green with the change. Do not skip the red step for “trivial” helpers.

## Keeping Tests Clean

Specs are first-class code. Prefer named harness helpers over giant `it` bodies. Do not leave commented-out tests (gated by ESLint).

## Tests Enable the -ilities

Trusted, readable specs are what make Plan / domain / store refactors safe.

## Clean Tests

- Behavior sentences for `it` titles (`'soft-deletes so list hides the row…'`), not `should` boilerplate.
- Prefer `it` consistently (gated). Use `describe` for the unit or feature slice under test.

### AAA

Arrange / Act / Assert. Separate phases with a single blank line when the body is more than a few lines. Gather values needed for asserts (store lists, DOM reads into locals) in Act — do not put statements other than `expect` after the assert block starts.

## Domain-Specific Testing Language

- Store: `useDocumentStoreHarness` (no TestBed) vs `provideDocumentStoreHarness` (TestBed + `DOCUMENT_STORE`) from `document-store.harness.ts`.
- Feature harnesses: `*.harness.ts` next to the component (e.g. `appHarness`, `planHarness`, `planAmountGridHarness`, settings / category-section / allocation-status harnesses). Prefer `aria-label` / `data-*` selectors.
- Cross-feature harness helpers live under `src/app/shared/harness/` as `*.harness.ts` (not in production `shared/helpers/`).
- Keep describe-local helpers only when they are not reused and the file stays small.

## Dual Standard

Specs may be longer and more linear than production. Ch.3 `complexity` / `max-depth` / `max-params` / `max-lines-per-function` stay off for `*.{spec,harness}.ts`. Named param object types (`no-restricted-syntax`) still apply; avoid copy-paste that trips `jscpd`.

## Coverage (Ch.17 T2)

Use `npm run test:coverage` (`ng test --coverage` via `@vitest/coverage-v8`). CI runs coverage on the test job. Pre-commit keeps bare `npm test` (no instrumentation). When debugging failures, use coverage patterns (T8) to see what the suite did not exercise.

## One Assert / Single Concept

Prefer the fewest expects that prove one outcome. Multiple expects are fine for one concept (e.g. insert metadata fields), capped at 4 per `it` (gated by `vitest/max-expects`). Split when one `it` packs unrelated stories or would exceed the cap. Type tables (`forEach` / `it.each`) that share one behavior stay acceptable.

## F.I.R.S.T.

- **Fast** — in-memory `fake-indexeddb`; unique DB per test; no real network/timers.
- **Independent** — no `.only`; fresh store via harness seam `beforeEach` / dispose in `afterEach`.
- **Repeatable** — always dispose IndexedDB; no order dependence across `it`s.
- **Self-validating** — every test asserts (gated: `expect-expect`, `valid-expect`, `no-conditional-expect`).
- **Timely** — write or adjust specs with the production change.

## Spec DOM trains

`fixture.nativeElement.querySelector…` is accepted harness style (not production LoD). Put trains behind named helpers in `*.harness.ts` rather than inline multi-hop chains in the `it` body. Do not require `By.css` or a page-object framework.
